<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pompeius Trogus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Gnaeus Pompeius Trogus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gnaeus Pompeius Trogus was a Roman historian of the Augustan age from the Vocontii of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-narbonensis">Gallia Narbonensis</a>, whose grandfather had received Roman citizenship from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>. His Philippic Histories, a universal history in 44 books centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and the Hellenistic kingdoms, is lost but survives in an abridgement by Justin, an important source for Hellenistic history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompeius-trogus.jpg" alt="Pompeius Trogus" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pompeius_Trogus_1777_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
